l evaluations**. `episode_6_index.json`, `episode6_official_summary.json`, and `episode_6_final_selection.json` summarize them. Builders, fresh-process timing logs, source files and unchanged official reports remain under `/tmp/research_history`. `episode_6_working_notes.md` records chronology. One hard-only builder syntax error was caught before executing anycase; original invalid builder and initial sources are preserved before the correction.\n\n`screen_all.py` compares against outputs previously computed from saved canonical initial implementation using only publicarrays; those caches are local research artifacts and never used inside submitted method. Local screens are not evaluator scores. Fresh benchmarkround5 had unusually large externalhost timingnoise, preserved in its rawtimelists. Official evaluations had no concurrent own numerical workloads.\n\n## Continuation\nStart from exact selected source and profile before extending. General sparseclass graphs, full segmented NumPy, Gaussian conditional point approximations, grouped point solves, and shared geometry were extensively explored this episode; repeating them without a materially new mechanism is unlikely useful. Exact rowenergy reduction is mathematically sound; whether it wins depends on kernel layout and reductioncost. Keep finite canonical annealing conventions: solving to convergence or removing all coarse class soft transforms changes the operator. Improvements must pass all30 gates and complete real `solve.sh` protocol before retention.\n\nNo protected assets or frozen launcher changed. No protected targets, private inputs, evaluator source, other trajectories, credentials, environment variables, network, external package installation or subagents accessed. Submission has exactly method.py and frozen solve.sh as root files; generated method cache removed. No evaluation pending.\n\nFinal diagnostic profile on public303_gaussian016:0.0754478seconds including profiling overhead, class transport0.033, point duals0.025, coupling0.007. This is not an evaluator score. Final source hash and frozen launcher hash verified, root submission files exactly method.py and solve.sh, and no evaluation pending. The selected source improves historical best time by2.9017percent and the episode6 start-source repeat by10.3279percent; compare full protocol results because timing noise is substantial.\n---history---\n/tmp/research_history/bench_episode6_round5_fresh.log\n/tmp/research_history/297_class_moment1_1/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/screen_all_295_308.log\n/tmp/research_history/369_exact_energy_contraction_numpy/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/292_take_shared_geometry_numpy/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/089_subsample_coupling_8/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/build_episode4_combinations.py\n/tmp/research_history/271_class_moment2_2/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/352_absolute_mass_both/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/222_coreset64_moment1/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/227_numpy_coreset80/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/216_hybrid_coupling_sum/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/episode_5_index.json\n/tmp/research_history/screen_all_313_336.log\n/tmp/research_history/157_fused_numpy_point_scaling/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/screen_all_361_365.log\n/tmp/research_history/068_skip_coarse_4_late_3/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/031_torch_geometry/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/208_coreset32/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/208_coreset32/construction_before_scope_fix.py\n/tmp/research_history/090_reuse_initial_kernel/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/129_packed_class_geometry/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/225_meanvariance_initial/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/117_omit_norm_relative_check/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/seed_303_gaussian_008_canonical.npy\n/tmp/research_history/build_episode5_analytic_initial.py\n/tmp/research_history/029_one_thread/method.py\n/tmp/research_history/screen_all_038_043.log\n/tmp/research_history/build_episode5_coupling_co